    </section>


    <!-- ARTICLES -->

    <article class="information" id="fuel">

        <h2>
            Why do fuel prices matter?
        </h2>

        <p>
            Fuel is used in transportation and in the movement
            of products from producers and suppliers to consumers.
            Changes in fuel prices may therefore affect transportation
            and delivery expenses. Monitoring price information can
            help consumers understand changes that may influence
            their household spending.
        </p>

    </article>


    <article class="information" id="budget">

        <h2>
            Plan before you shop
        </h2>

        <p>
            Checking prices before visiting a market or store
            gives consumers a reference for preparing their budget.
            Actual prices may vary depending on location, seller,
            product quality, and other market conditions.
        </p>

    </article>


    <!-- SOURCES -->

    <section class="sources">

        <h2>About the Price Information</h2>

        <p>
            PresyoCheck is an academic prototype designed to
            present price information in a simple and accessible
            format.
        </p>

        <ul>
            <li>Prices should be verified using reliable sources.</li>
            <li>Prices may differ between locations and sellers.</li>
            <li>Displayed values should include their corresponding date.</li>
        </ul>

    </section>

</main>


<footer>

    <strong>PresyoCheck</strong>

    <p>
